# mp-acq-genmc.kat: x := 1 (e0) is in a hole before the acquire read e1 and
# z := 1 (e2), which a := z (e4) reads; b := x (e5) reads 0. Without e0 the
# graph is consistent; with it, e5 -fr-> e0 -[W];po;[ACQ];po;[W]-> e2 -rfe->
# e4 -[ACQ];po-> e5 is a cycle, and e0, the only write to x, has no other
# place in mo.
e0: T0 W(x) rlx
e1: T0 R(y) acq
e2: T0 W(z) rlx
e3: T1 TB acq
e4: T1 R(z) acq
e5: T1 R(x) rlx
rf: e2->e4
mo(x): e0
mo(z): e2
